course: dictionary
lesson: 11171
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word wine can name a drink, a dark red colour, or a fancy meal. Read the words around it to find out which. «Many grown-ups drink things that change how they feel» tells you wine is a drink, and that drink is for grown-ups.
explain: «The bubbles in sparkling wine are made by yeast inside the bottle» is about the drink. Wine can also describe a colour, as in wine-red. Ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Wine is an adult drink, and alcohol can harm the body, so children must never drink it. Context helps you find a meaning, but safety rules always come first.
fact: Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grapes, or sometimes other fruits.
fact: Fermenting means yeast turns sugar into alcohol.
fact: Wine can also mean a dark red colour, as in wine-red.
fact: To wine and dine someone means to take them out for a fancy meal and treat them well.
fact: Alcohol is for adults only, and it can harm the body.
exercise: «Greeks sailed in triremes and traded olive oil, wine and pottery.» In this sentence, what is wine? | A colour | A fancy meal | *A drink | A kind of ship
exercise: Mum wore a wine-red dress to the party. What does wine-red describe? | *A dark red colour | A type of party game | A sweet fruit | A glass of drink
exercise: Grandad said he would wine and dine Nana on her birthday. What does wine and dine mean? | *Take her out for a fancy meal and treat her well | Drink wine in the garden | Buy her a new pair of shoes | Tell her a funny joke
test: «The Gospels tell of amazing things Jesus did: turning water into wine.» What is wine in this sentence? | A cup | A colour | *A drink | A meal
test: Why must children never drink wine? | It is too cold | It is too sweet | It is only sold in summer | *Alcohol is for adults and can harm the body
exam: In «a glass of wine» at dinner for grown-ups, what does wine mean? | To treat someone to a meal | A type of glass | *An alcoholic drink | A dark red colour
